STACK EDITOR - a Swing text editor built on stacks
===================================================

HOW TO RUN (pick one)
  1. Double-click StackEditor.jar            (needs Java 11+ installed)
  2. Double-click run.bat (Windows) or run ./run.sh (Mac/Linux)
  3. Open the "src" folder in IntelliJ IDEA, Eclipse or NetBeans and run
     stackeditor.Main

HOW TO USE
  - Type in the left pane. Every edit is pushed on the UNDO stack.
  - Undo (Ctrl+Z) pops the undo stack and pushes the edit onto the REDO stack.
  - Redo (Ctrl+Y or Ctrl+Shift+Z) moves it back.
  - Typing something new clears the redo stack.
  - The status bar uses a BRACKET stack to check (), [] and {}.
    The first error is highlighted in red in the text.
  - The right-hand panels show all three stacks live (top is listed first).
  - "Load sample" inserts balanced code; delete a } to see an error.

FILES
  ArrayStack.java     hand-written generic stack (push, pop, peek)
  EditAction.java     one edit (offset, removed text, inserted text)
  BracketChecker.java bracket matching with a stack
  EditorFrame.java    the Swing window, undo/redo logic
  Main.java           entry point
